{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/category_toolbar

    The toolbar of the category showcase: a real GET form that works with
    JavaScript off, in two rows and a count line. Row one narrows: the search
    box, the favourites toggle, and one disclosure holding every other filter
    there is - the state group, one group per allowlisted custom field, and the
    start-date range with its quick options. Row two organises: the three sort chips as a radio group whose
    legend reads inline before them, the card/list toggle (two submit buttons
    carrying the view parameter) and core's own action menu for the category's
    managers. The count line comes third: its number in bold, the sentence,
    "see all as a list" when a narrowed page spreads its results over areas, and
    the way out of every filter right after it.

    Each group names itself once: the legend is both what a screen reader
    announces for the fieldset and what the design shows beside the pills.

    The filter disclosure is a native details element, so it opens, closes and
    announces itself with no script. It is rendered open when a filter it holds
    narrows the listing - not for a search alone, which shows in its own box -
    and the number of active filters is printed on its summary, because a
    reader who collapses it has to see that the page is still narrowed. The
    summary's word has a span of its own because at a phone's width the
    stylesheet hides that span alone, keeping the icon, the count badge and the
    accessible name.

    The quick date options are ordinary links carrying the two parameters the
    date fields carry, computed on the server in the site's timezone. Either
    date field may be left empty: each bound narrows on its own. The calendar
    is the client's (category_daterange) and speaks the same parameters: it
    mounts its start and end boxes into the empty dim-daterange region, hides the native
    fields (dim-dateinputs) and reads three facts off this markup rather than
    computing them - the first weekday and today's date from the date fieldset,
    and each quick option's bounds from its link - so the client does no
    timezone arithmetic. The range it holds is also drawn as a removable pill in
    the count row, the one part of the toolbar a reader who collapsed the
    filters can still see: it mounts into the empty dim-daterange-pill region.

    The count is a live region the client rewrites in place. It is rendered here
    so the design's count row exists, and Mustache resolves its values up the
    context stack from the listing that includes this partial. It is written on
    one source line, because Behat's text assertions do not normalise
    whitespace, and each of its parts carries a region the client rewrites - the
    number, the sentence, the "see all as a list" link and the note the
    automatic opening of an area appends. The number is never hidden on the
    server: it is always a formatted number, and a zero is a string an inverted
    section would treat as empty.

    The badge on the Filter summary (dim-filtercount) counts the applied filters
    and is the only number of this toolbar visible while the panel is shut. Each
    of its two halves - the digit sighted readers see and the sentence a screen
    reader is read - carries a region, because the client rewrites both after
    every request; the badge is hidden while the number is zero.

    Every element the client updates in place is always in the document, hidden
    when it has nothing to say, so the client need not know how to build it: a
    pill's count (dim-pill-count; post-filter, and an option without a count
    shows its label alone, never a zero), the too-short-search notice
    (dim-toolbar-notice) and the "clear filters" link (dim-vitrine-clear), which
    stays a link so it works with the module switched off and carries the
    dim-clear action every "clear filters" control of the page shares. Each
    filter group's fieldset repeats its radio group's name in a data attribute,
    so the client finds the group a returned option belongs to without parsing
    an id, and the pill track is named dim-pill-track so a pill the client
    creates lands inside it. The view buttons carry the dim-view action, by
    which the client suppresses their submit and swaps a class. The organisation
    group, the filter disclosure and the date fieldset are dim-sort, dim-filters
    and dim-date.

    The submit buttons stay inside the form because the template lint renders
    this partial on its own. The first submit of the form is a name-less,
    visually hidden one: Enter in the search box presses the form's first
    submit, and the view buttons carry a name and a value that would otherwise
    flip the reader's view. Two more submits are hidden once the client module
    runs - one beside the organisation chips, one inside the filter panel -
    because a reader without that module has to be able to commit a choice made
    in either row.

    While a panel of the areas is open, hidden fields carry it (open, and psort
    when the panel is in name order), so a filter or a view submitted without
    JavaScript keeps the panel open; each names its own region, because the
    client modules keep them in step with the address.

    On a phone the view toggle joins the search line: the two view buttons are
    written twice, on the search line after the filter disclosure
    (dim-view-phone, icon-only, the word visually hidden) and in the organising
    row (dim-view-row, glyph and word), so the document order is the screen
    order at every width. The stylesheet shows one copy per breakpoint and hides
    the other entirely, out of the tab order and the accessibility tree. The
    phone copy comes first in the document, so anything addressing the visible
    toggle at a desktop width scopes to dim-view-row.

    The favourites toggle (dim-line-star) sits on the search line right before
    the filter disclosure, drawn only for a reader who has favourites. It
    combines with the state rather than being one of its values, so it is a
    submit button of its own: it posts fav with the value a press turns it to,
    and aria-pressed says whether it is on. While it is on, a hidden field
    (dim-fav-field) earlier in the form carries fav=1, so every other submission
    keeps it; a press that turns it off posts both, and the button's value comes
    last, which is the one the server reads. The client enables and disables
    that field as it toggles the button (dim-fav). The glyph is the course card's
    own star, solid when pressed; the word and the number of favourites are the
    button's accessible name (dim-fav-count) and its tooltip names it. The form
    carries dim-toolbar--hasstar while it is drawn, so the stylesheet can make
    room for it on the line.

    The hidden list carries whatever identifies the category on the shell that
    is drawing, and may be empty: a GET submission replaces the action's query
    string, so on the anonymous shell's route the id is a path segment of the
    action and the form needs no field of its own. The control ids are built from
    the category id on the server.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "action": "https://example.com/course/index.php",
        "hidden": [{"name": "categoryid", "value": 7}],
        "formid": "dim-vitrine-form-7",
        "searchid": "dim-vitrine-q-7",
        "searchname": "q",
        "searchlabel": "Buscar cursos",
        "searchplaceholder": "Buscar pelo nome",
        "query": "resgate",
        "searchtooshort": false,
        "searchtooshortlabel": "Digite pelo menos 2 caracteres para buscar.",
        "sortgroup": {
            "legend": "Organizar",
            "name": "sort",
            "options": [
                {"id": "dim-sort-7-category", "value": "category", "label": "Por categoria", "checked": true},
                {"id": "dim-sort-7-name", "value": "name", "label": "A-Z", "checked": false},
                {"id": "dim-sort-7-recent", "value": "recent", "label": "Recentes", "checked": false}
            ]
        },
        "sortapplylabel": "Aplicar",
        "statusgroup": {
            "legend": "Situação",
            "name": "chip",
            "options": [
                {"id": "dim-chip-7-all", "value": "", "label": "Todos", "count": 14, "hascount": true, "checked": true},
                {"id": "dim-chip-7-enrolled", "value": "enrolled", "label": "Meus cursos", "count": 3, "hascount": true, "checked": false}
            ]
        },
        "hasstatusgroup": true,
        "favourites": {"name": "fav", "value": 1, "pressed": false, "count": 2, "label": "Favoritos"},
        "hasfavourites": true,
        "facets": [
            {
                "legend": "Modalidade",
                "name": "cf_12",
                "anyid": "dim-cf-12-any",
                "anylabel": "Todos",
                "anychecked": true,
                "options": [
                    {"id": "dim-cf-12-1", "value": 1, "label": "Online", "count": 9, "hascount": true, "checked": false},
                    {"id": "dim-cf-12-2", "value": 2, "label": "Presencial", "count": 5, "hascount": true, "checked": false}
                ]
            }
        ],
        "hasfacets": true,
        "datefromid": "dim-datefrom-7",
        "datetoid": "dim-dateto-7",
        "datefromname": "from",
        "datetoname": "to",
        "datefrom": "2026-09-17",
        "dateto": "2026-09-24",
        "datelegend": "Data de início",
        "datefromlabel": "Início",
        "datetolabel": "Fim",
        "firstday": 0,
        "today": "2026-09-18",
        "datequick": [
            {"label": "Hoje", "url": "https://example.com/course/index.php?categoryid=7&from=2026-09-17&to=2026-09-17", "from": "2026-09-17", "to": "2026-09-17", "current": false},
            {"label": "Esta semana", "url": "https://example.com/course/index.php?categoryid=7&from=2026-09-14&to=2026-09-20", "from": "2026-09-14", "to": "2026-09-20", "current": true}
        ],
        "filtercount": 2,
        "hasfiltercount": true,
        "filtercountlabel": "Filtros aplicados: 2",
        "pagesizename": "perpage",
        "pagesize": 24,
        "haspagesize": true,
        "openfields": [
            {"name": "open", "value": 8, "region": "dim-open-field"},
            {"name": "psort", "value": "name", "region": "dim-psort-field"}
        ],
        "viewname": "view",
        "viewlabel": "Exibição",
        "views": [
            {"value": "cards", "label": "Cartões", "current": true, "icon": "fa-border-all"},
            {"value": "list", "label": "Lista", "current": false, "icon": "fa-list"}
        ],
        "submitlabel": "Filtrar",
        "filtersopen": true,
        "countnumber": "16",
        "countline": "cursos para “resgate”: 2 nesta categoria e 14 em 4 áreas",
        "seeallurl": "https://example.com/course/index.php?categoryid=7&q=resgate&sort=recent",
        "hasfilters": true,
        "clearurl": "https://example.com/course/index.php?categoryid=7",
        "clearlabel": "Limpar filtros",
        "manageactions": "<div class=\"action-menu\"><a href=\"#\">Manage courses</a></div>",
        "hasmanageactions": true
    }
}}
<form class="dim-toolbar{{#hasfavourites}} dim-toolbar--hasstar{{/hasfavourites}}" id="{{formid}}" method="get" action="{{action}}" data-region="dim-vitrine-toolbar">
    {{#hidden}}<input type="hidden" name="{{name}}" value="{{value}}">{{/hidden}}
    {{#haspagesize}}
    <input type="hidden" name="{{pagesizename}}" value="{{pagesize}}">
    {{/haspagesize}}
    {{#openfields}}
    <input type="hidden" name="{{name}}" value="{{value}}" data-region="{{region}}">
    {{/openfields}}
    {{#favourites}}
    <input type="hidden" name="{{name}}" value="1" data-region="dim-fav-field"{{^pressed}} disabled{{/pressed}}>
    {{/favourites}}
    <button type="submit" class="visually-hidden dim-toolbar__defaultsubmit" tabindex="-1">{{submitlabel}}</button>
    <div class="dim-toolbar__row dim-toolbar__row--narrow">
        <div class="dim-toolbar__search">
            <label class="visually-hidden" for="{{searchid}}">{{searchlabel}}</label>
            <i class="fa fa-magnifying-glass dim-toolbar__searchicon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <input class="form-control dim-toolbar__input" type="search" id="{{searchid}}" name="{{searchname}}" value="{{query}}" placeholder="{{searchplaceholder}}" autocomplete="off">
        </div>
        {{#favourites}}
        <button type="submit" class="dim-toolbar__star" name="{{name}}" value="{{value}}" aria-pressed="{{#pressed}}true{{/pressed}}{{^pressed}}false{{/pressed}}" title="{{label}}" data-action="dim-fav" data-region="dim-line-star"><i class="{{#pressed}}fa-solid{{/pressed}}{{^pressed}}fa-regular{{/pressed}} fa-star" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden">{{label}} <span data-region="dim-fav-count">{{count}}</span></span></button>
        {{/favourites}}
        <details class="dim-toolbar__filters" data-region="dim-filters"{{#filtersopen}} open{{/filtersopen}}>
            <summary class="dim-toolbar__filterstoggle"><i class="fa fa-filter" aria-hidden="true"></i> <span class="dim-toolbar__filterslabel">{{submitlabel}}</span> <span class="dim-toolbar__filtercount" data-region="dim-filtercount"{{^hasfiltercount}} hidden{{/hasfiltercount}}><span aria-hidden="true" data-region="dim-filtercount-number">{{filtercount}}</span><span class="visually-hidden" data-region="dim-filtercount-label">{{filtercountlabel}}</span></span></summary>
            <div class="dim-toolbar__panel">
                {{#statusgroup}}
                <fieldset class="dim-toolbar__group" data-region="dim-vitrine-group" data-name="{{name}}">
                    <legend class="dim-toolbar__grouplabel">{{legend}}</legend>
                    <div class="dim-toolbar__pills" data-region="dim-pill-track">
                        {{#options}}
                        <input class="dim-pill__input visually-hidden" type="radio" name="{{name}}" id="{{id}}" value="{{value}}"{{#checked}} checked{{/checked}}>
                        <label class="dim-pill" for="{{id}}">{{label}} <span class="dim-pill__count" data-region="dim-pill-count"{{^hascount}} hidden{{/hascount}}>{{count}}</span></label>
                        {{/options}}
                    </div>
                </fieldset>
                {{/statusgroup}}
                {{#facets}}
                <fieldset class="dim-toolbar__group" data-region="dim-vitrine-group" data-name="{{name}}">
                    <legend class="dim-toolbar__grouplabel">{{legend}}</legend>
                    <div class="dim-toolbar__pills" data-region="dim-pill-track">
                        <input class="dim-pill__input visually-hidden" type="radio" name="{{name}}" id="{{anyid}}" value="0"{{#anychecked}} checked{{/anychecked}}>
                        <label class="dim-pill" for="{{anyid}}">{{anylabel}}</label>
                        {{#options}}
                        <input class="dim-pill__input visually-hidden" type="radio" name="{{name}}" id="{{id}}" value="{{value}}"{{#checked}} checked{{/checked}}>
                        <label class="dim-pill" for="{{id}}">{{label}} <span class="dim-pill__count" data-region="dim-pill-count"{{^hascount}} hidden{{/hascount}}>{{count}}</span></label>
                        {{/options}}
                    </div>
                </fieldset>
                {{/facets}}
                <fieldset class="dim-toolbar__group dim-toolbar__group--date" data-region="dim-date" data-firstday="{{firstday}}" data-today="{{today}}">
                    <legend class="dim-toolbar__grouplabel">{{datelegend}}</legend>
                    <div class="dim-toolbar__daterange" data-region="dim-daterange"></div>
                    <div class="dim-toolbar__dates" data-region="dim-dateinputs">
                        <div class="dim-toolbar__datefield">
                            <label class="dim-toolbar__datelabel" for="{{datefromid}}">{{datefromlabel}}</label>
                            <input class="form-control dim-toolbar__dateinput" type="date" id="{{datefromid}}" name="{{datefromname}}" value="{{datefrom}}">
                        </div>
                        <div class="dim-toolbar__datefield">
                            <label class="dim-toolbar__datelabel" for="{{datetoid}}">{{datetolabel}}</label>
                            <input class="form-control dim-toolbar__dateinput" type="date" id="{{datetoid}}" name="{{datetoname}}" value="{{dateto}}">
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <ul class="dim-toolbar__quick" role="list">
                        {{#datequick}}
                        <li><a class="dim-quick{{#current}} dim-quick--on{{/current}}" href="{{url}}" data-action="dim-quick" data-from="{{from}}" data-to="{{to}}"{{#current}} aria-current="true"{{/current}}>{{label}}</a></li>
                        {{/datequick}}
                    </ul>
                </fieldset>
                <div class="dim-toolbar__actions">
                    <button type="submit" class="dim-toolbar__submit dim-nojs-only">{{submitlabel}}</button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </details>
        <div class="dim-toolbar__view dim-toolbar__view--phone" role="group" aria-label="{{viewlabel}}" data-region="dim-view-phone">
            {{#views}}
            <button type="submit" class="dim-toolbar__viewbtn" data-action="dim-view" name="{{viewname}}" value="{{value}}" aria-pressed="{{#current}}true{{/current}}{{^current}}false{{/current}}" title="{{label}}"><i class="fa {{icon}}" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden">{{label}}</span></button>
            {{/views}}
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="dim-toolbar__notice" role="status" data-region="dim-toolbar-notice"{{^searchtooshort}} hidden{{/searchtooshort}}>{{searchtooshortlabel}}</p>
    <div class="dim-toolbar__row dim-toolbar__row--organise">
        {{#sortgroup}}
        <fieldset class="dim-toolbar__group dim-toolbar__group--sort" data-region="dim-sort" data-name="{{name}}">
            <legend class="dim-toolbar__grouplabel">{{legend}}</legend>
            <div class="dim-toolbar__pills">
                {{#options}}
                <input class="dim-pill__input visually-hidden" type="radio" name="{{name}}" id="{{id}}" value="{{value}}"{{#checked}} checked{{/checked}}>
                <label class="dim-pill" for="{{id}}">{{label}}</label>
                {{/options}}
            </div>
        </fieldset>
        {{/sortgroup}}
        <button type="submit" class="dim-toolbar__sortsubmit dim-nojs-only">{{sortapplylabel}}</button>
        <div class="dim-toolbar__view" role="group" aria-label="{{viewlabel}}" data-region="dim-view-row">
            {{#views}}
            <button type="submit" class="dim-toolbar__viewbtn" data-action="dim-view" name="{{viewname}}" value="{{value}}" aria-pressed="{{#current}}true{{/current}}{{^current}}false{{/current}}"><i class="fa {{icon}}" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="dim-toolbar__viewlabel">{{label}}</span></button>
            {{/views}}
        </div>
        {{#hasmanageactions}}
        <div class="dim-toolbar__manage">{{{manageactions}}}</div>
        {{/hasmanageactions}}
    </div>
    <div class="dim-toolbar__row dim-toolbar__row--count">
        <p class="dim-vitrine__count" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-region="dim-vitrine-count"><b class="dim-vitrine__countnumber" data-region="dim-vitrine-countnumber">{{countnumber}}</b> <span data-region="dim-vitrine-counttext">{{countline}}</span><span class="dim-vitrine__seeall" data-region="dim-vitrine-seeall"{{^seeallurl}} hidden{{/seeallurl}}> · <a href="{{seeallurl}}">{{#str}}category_seeaslist, theme_dimensions{{/str}}</a></span><span class="dim-vitrine__countnote" data-region="dim-vitrine-countnote" hidden>. <span data-region="dim-vitrine-countnotetext"></span></span></p>
        <div class="dim-toolbar__pillbar" data-region="dim-daterange-pill"></div>
        <a class="dim-toolbar__clear" href="{{clearurl}}" data-region="dim-vitrine-clear" data-action="dim-clear"{{^hasfilters}} hidden{{/hasfilters}}>{{clearlabel}}</a>
    </div>
</form>
